 :why-this-slice-exists
 "Slice 7's NEXT SLICE note ends the row with a PROSE CLAIM: `nothing in the
  acceptance is left that a lane can take without a ruling` and `the row is
  waiting on Joe, not on work`. Setting :F11 to :blocked on the strength of that
  sentence would be the ledger accepting an assertion where it demands a run
  record everywhere else. The sibling row :F12 did not do that: it mechanised the
  same claim into runs/F12-organise/15-remainder.edn (:remainder-fully-gated?
  true, :obligations-not-satisfied-and-not-gated []) and its :blocker cites the
  artifact rather than restating it (worklist.edn :F12 :blocker). This slice owes
  :F11 the same artifact. Registering a choice or an arm is NOT a ruling -- this
  row has registered three -- so an unmet obligation with no gate is LANE WORK,
  not Joe's."
