   `laws stated in Lean` is unmet on F3's account, the gate for it may not exist
   as a priced arm -- and completing a pricing is lane work."
  :what-refutation-would-mean
  "If either candidate is adjudicated UNMET AND UNGATED, slice 7's closing claim
   is refuted, :F11 is NOT waiting on Joe, and the row's next slice is the work
   the check names. If both are adjudicated satisfied or gated, the premise
   holds, the artifact licenses :blocked, and slice 9 is the decision sheet."}
 :measurements-asked
 {:M1 "The DECOMPOSITION, anchored not invented. Read :F11's :acceptance from
       worklist.edn. Split it into clauses and locate each obligation by a
       VERBATIM SUBSTRING of that acceptance, recording the substring and its
       character offset, exactly as f12_remainder_check.bb:26-31 and :86-96 do.
       An obligation whose substring is not found is a script FAILURE, not a
       measurement -- the decomposition must be provably a decomposition of the
       committed text."
  :M2 "SATISFACTION, decided from the tree. For each obligation decide satisfied
       / not-satisfied from artifacts under mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/ and
       runs/F11-find/, each verdict carrying its file:line or run-record pointer,
       or `not found`. Absence of a witness is a MEASUREMENT, not an error
       (f12_remainder_check.bb:61-68 states that rule); do not throw on it."
  :M3 "GATING, with the gate QUOTED FROM THE LIVE REGISTRY. For each unmet
       obligation name the choice key that gates it and a fragment of that
       entry's :question, and CHECK the fragment against the live
       aif-equations.edn before it may count as a gate -- f12_remainder_check.bb
       :33-45 is the pattern and its comment states why. A gate whose fragment no
       longer occurs in the live entry must FAIL, not silently pass. A gating
       choice must additionally be verified :observed-not-decided with no :ruling
       key; a RULED choice does not gate anything."
  :M4 "THE VERDICT, and it must be able to come out FALSE. Emit
       :obligations-not-satisfied-and-not-gated as an explicit vector and
       :remainder-fully-gated? as its emptiness. Adjudicate the two named
       candidate refuters (i) and (ii) above EXPLICITLY, each as its own key with
       its own pointers, and record the verdict whichever way it falls. Do not
       tune the obligation set until the vector empties -- if the honest
       decomposition leaves an obligation unmet and ungated, THAT IS THE RESULT."
  :M5 "Determinism: the artifact reproduces BYTE-IDENTICALLY over two runs, and
       the checker reports its own sha256."}
 :inhabitance-and-nondegeneracy-floor-demanded-in-advance
 "This is the NINTH consecutive slice across :F11/:F12 in which review has had to
  supply this floor, and this slice's degenerate failure has a specific shape:
  a checker that computes :remainder-fully-gated? true VACUOUSLY -- by an
  obligation set so coarse that nothing can be unmet, by a gating table that
  matches any choice, or by treating `no witness found` as `satisfied`. So:
  every obligation must be shown SEPARATING, by a control that makes exactly that
  obligation flip; the gating fragments must be shown checked, by a control that
  perturbs a fragment and observes the FAILURE; and the verdict must be shown
  able to be false, by a control that removes a gate and observes
  :remainder-fully-gated? go false with the obligation named in the vector."
